# The "*" is replaced by the  display number of the X server. 
# For example, if the X server is invoked using the command X :0, the 
# X0devices file is used.

# This X*devices file defines the input devices opened by the X server 
# during initialization.

# This file is not required.  The X server correctly initializes itself 
# and chooses default input devices as best as possible
# if this file does not exist.
#
# If the machine on which the X server is running supports input
# devices via the DIN interface, the DIN keyboard and mouse will be used
# as the default X keyboard and pointer devices.
#
# This is an example of a valid X*devices file.
# Not all of the following entries would normally be in the same file.
# Entries can be in any order, HOWEVER,
# Where conflicts occur, the last conflicting entry is used.

# Blank lines and comments (text following a '#') are ignored.
# Each entry occupies a single line.
# Fields in an entry are separated by spaces or tabs.

#******************************************************************************
#
# The X server can be configured to initialize itself with no input devices:
#

#first	NULL	keyboard		# the X keyboard is a null device
#first	NULL	pointer  		# the X pointer is a null device


#******************************************************************************
#
# Some RS-232 input devices are supported by dynamically loaded drivers.
# The driver specified by the "Name" keyword must reside in the directory
# /usr/X11R6/hp/lib/extensions.
#

#******************************************************************************
#
# To use input devices as the X pointer or X keyboard, specify
# "Pointer" or "Keyboard" with the "Use" keyword.
#

#Begin_Device_Description
#Name	driver.1
#Use	Pointer
#Path	/dev/ttyS1
#End_Device_Description

#******************************************************************************
#
# To merge the input from these devices with that from the X pointer or X 
# keyboard, specify "Other" with the "Use" keyword.
#

#Begin_Device_Description
#Name	driver.1
#Use	Other
#Path	/dev/ttyS1
#End_Device_Description

#******************************************************************************
# 
# To configure the Xserver to use a Wacom tablet (Intuos model), uncomment
# the following lines below.  The "Path" may need to change depending on
# which serial port the tablet is connected.  The "Use Other" specification
# will merge the tablet with that of the X pointer.  To access the tablet
# as an XInput extension device, change that line to be "Use Extension".
#
#Begin_Device_Description
#Name   wacom.1
#Use    Other
#Path   /dev/ttyS1
#End_Device_Description

